// The strolls: each level's human-possible 100% run made calm, for the game playing itself behind
// the console's home (attract.wrela): its twitches smoothed into plain running wherever the run
// still finishes, and pauses where it stops to look, each made up (route/stroll.wrela). No person
// has played them. `wrela tool route -- --stroll` writes this file again from routes_<key>.wrela's
// `HUMAN_FULL`; run it again when a level's human runs change.

use course::{HOME, WETLANDS, SAVANNA, RAINFOREST, AVIARY, REPTILES, POLAR, FARM, FOOD_COURT, course}
use pad::{DOWN, Hold, JUMP, LEFT, PRESS, RIGHT, UP, hold}
use world::play

